  "linked_issues": [
    {
      "body": "Since Python 3.3, the stdlib provides the function `shutil.get_terminal_size()`. Now that the project has dropped Python 2\r\nsupport, the compatibility shim is no longer necessary.\r\n\r\nThe stdlib version returns a named tuple. So rather than indexing \"0\", can use the more self-documenting attribute \"columns\".\r\n\r\nDocs available at: https://docs.python.org/3/library/shutil.html#shutil.get_terminal_size\r\n",
      "number": 1736,
      "url": "https://github.com/pallets/click/issues/1736"
    }
  ],
